 "b_note": "A standard radiation era has H*age = 1/2 and H/H_standard(T) = 1. \"formed?\" cases: vacuum-dominated from the start; rho_V falls only to ~9 M^4/(4 gamma N). Prepared case: the dissipation is negligible and the final total vacuum energy is what was prepared. Relaxed-before-EW case: the EW and QCD plateaux are released after the relaxation, total -> -(D_EW + D_QCD) < 0, turnaround and crunch. kappa = 1e-3 from 1e18 GeV: drain gamma kappa^2 H_i^4/32 = 3.9e62 GeV^4, so the prepared value would also have to absorb it.",
